Data cleaning using the Tidyverse and Janitor

# Introduction

This session will touch on different functions you can use from the tidyverse suite of packages, and the janitor package. We will also be using the 'Messy' package to (as you would expect) turn some of the base R datasets into a mess for cleaning practice. 

There are many resources available, but the information on Data tidying is primarily derived from [R for Data Science (2e)](https://r4ds.hadley.nz/)



